## Phase 5: Document & conclude

Create `EXPERIMENT_REPORT.md`:

```markdown
# Experiment Report: Impact of Guidance Specificity on LLM Editorial Output

## Hypothesis
IF specific numeric targets (170–190 words)
THEN first-pass acceptance increases 30%+
Because explicit bounds are more computable

## Results
- Vague guidance: 28% first-pass acceptance
- Specific guidance: 76% first-pass acceptance
- Difference: 48 percentage points (χ² = 22.4, p < 0.001)

## Confidence
HIGH. Large effect size; statistically significant; reproducible.

## Implications
1. Update all guidance documents to include specific numeric targets
2. Prioritize: word count, title length, tag count
3. Test next: whether examples (showing title styles) further improve outcomes

## Failure modes to monitor
- Does Condition B guidance cause AI to pad weak content to hit word target?
- Are fields with fewer examples (metadata, tags) less responsive to specificity?

## Decision
ADOPT Condition B guidance. Roll out across team by 2026-04-01.

## Follow-up test
"Do exemplars improve metadata accuracy?"
```

