## Common pitfalls

| Pitfall | Sign | Fix |
|---------|------|-----|
| **Too small sample** | "We tested 10 items and got better" | Use 50+ per condition; don't generalize from small samples |
| **No control group** | "We changed guidance and output improved" | Always run A/B test (old vs. new) |
| **Confounding variables** | "We updated guidance AND trained editors AND new model" | Change one thing at a time |
| **Selection bias** | "We tested on easy examples" | Randomly assign examples across conditions |
| **Measuring the wrong thing** | "Editors say it's better" (subjective) | Track objective metrics (revision rate, time, accuracy) |
| **Not documenting assumptions** | "We concluded it works but no one remembers how" | Write EXPERIMENT_REPORT.md with all assumptions upfront |

